  // Ency entries
  "EncyPath_DownloadedData/Prototype": "Prototype Development",
  "EncyPath_DownloadedData/Prototype/ProtoUpgrades": "Prototype Vessel Upgrades",
  "EncyPath_DownloadedData/Prototype/ProtoTerminal": "Terminal Data",
  "EncyPath_DownloadedData/Prototype/Scanned": "Scanned Data",
  "EncyPath_DownloadedData/Prototype/AlienClues": "Alien Clues",

  "ProtoPrecursorIngotEncy_Title": "Almanite Framework",
  "ProtoPrecursorIngotEncy_Body": "An advanced material with high structural integrity. Its core, composed of charged almanite, stabilizes 8 external frames used for dynamic construction.\n\nAnalysis:\n- Unprecedented structural integrity\n- Used in reinforced alien construction\n- Requires multiple advanced materials",
  "ProtoCloakEncy_Title": "Light Distortion Field",
  "ProtoCloakEncy_Body": "This schematic provides missing data used by light refractors lining the hull of the Prototype. The refractors generate a radius around the Prototype whereby external light is dynamically bent around the submarine, making it difficult for aggressive fauna to hit.\n\nIt is clear that the intended use for this technology is to decrease the accuracy of aggressive fauna during emergency scenarios, and the reflective barrier does <b>NOT</b> appear to hinder fauna from initially detecting the Prototype through vibrations and sound.",
  "ProtoEmergencyWarpEncy_Title": "Emergency Warp Protocol",
  "ProtoEmergencyWarpEncy_Body": "This schematic contains a backdoor protocol for the Prototype's archway interceptor which enables it to instantaneously transport the vessel to a pre-specified location; Likely the submarine's point of construction.\n\n<b>Note: Due to the immense concentration of dark energy delegated to this protocol, it is likely that all on-board power will be consumed upon calling this protocol.</b>",
  "ProtoInterceptorEncy_Title": "UNUSED",
  "ProtoInterceptorEncy_Body": "UNUSED.",
  "ProtoRepairDroidsEncy_Title": "Repair Droids",
  "ProtoRepairDroidsEncy_Body": "This schematic details protocols enabling access to 4 autonomous maintenance robot assembly depots located in the Prototype’s upper stern. Autonomous repair droid construction schematics match data found in background scans of previously-discovered alien facilities.\n\nRepair droids possess advanced welding technology capable of repairing external hull damage over time.\nSafety protocols onboard maintenance robots prevent droid deployment during creature attacks.",
  "ProtoDepthOptimizersEncy_Title": "Depth Optimizers",
  "ProtoDepthOptimizersEncy_Body": "This protocol activates passive depth optimizers built into the hull of the Prototype. These optimizers semi-permanently reinforce the Prototype’s hull, allowing for near unlimited crush depth and greater efficiency at increased depths.",
  "ProtoIonBarrierEncy_Title": "Ion Barrier",
  "ProtoIonBarrierEncy_Body": "This schematic links ion energy emitters lining the hull of the Prototype. The generated energy field creates a thin electrostatic mesh surrounding the vessel capable of absorbing blunt force impacts. The maximum capacity for the energy cells powering the energy emitters is limited, meaning that the barrier may require time to recharge in-between activations and may only fully protect the vessel for a few seconds at a time. The barrier appears to be able to absorb impacts and re-direct their energy back into the Prototype.\n<b>Assessment: Consistent timing allows for power generation through repeated shock absorption</b>",
  "ProtoStasisPulseEncy_Title": "Stasis Pulse",
  "ProtoStasisPulseEncy_Body": "This schematic uses energy emitters lining the hull of the ship to passively collect and discharge electrostatic energy. The discharge of this energy  resembles the latest defensive developments in the <i>Survival-Grade Alterra Stasis Rifle</i>. Upon charge and activation, the electrostatic pulse will temporarily paralyse nearby biological tissues, some internal organs and all brain activity. Paralysis of nearby organisms is dependent on their size; Larger organisms may regain mental functioning faster than smaller ones.\n\n<b>Warning: Experiencing a discharge from this module may semi-permanently damage key cognitive functions such as muscle control, mental clarity and communication from the brain stem to vital and sensory organs causing potential brain death from cerebral hypoxia within 10 minutes of infliction. Avoid at all costs.</b>",
  "ProtoIonGeneratorEncy_Title": "Ion Generator",
  "ProtoIonGeneratorEncy_Body": "By re-routing power from all non-essential systems onboard the Prototype, this protocol initiates a fusion reaction in the ion reactor, which generates power over time. Due to the extreme conservation of power necessary to carry out the fusion reaction, several critical systems, such as movement and ability use, will be disabled while the generator is active.\n\n<b>Assessment: Use higher-capacity energy devices for maximum recharge efficiency.</b>",
  "ProtoDataStreamsEncy_Title": "Hydrodynamic Ventilation",
  "ProtoDataStreamsEncy_Body": "The Prototype features several water intake grills on its upper bow. This upgrade enhances said grills, allowing them to increase flow to the vessel's ion reactor. Doing so allows the vessel to more efficiently store and deploy energy to its secondary systems, including those delegated to other upgrades. When installed, the Hydrodynamic Ventilation system will reduce the cost of upgrades by 1 charge, and reduce the depletion-over-time of all upgrades by approximately 50%.\n\n<b>Assessment: Vital energy-saving measure. Highly recommended for long journeys.</b>",
  "ProtoArchwayOverrideEncy_Title": "Archway Override Protocol",
  "ProtoArchwayOverrideEncy_Body": "On the activation of this protocol, the Prototype's onboard teleporter connects to and re-routes the connection between any pair of activated alien teleporters, allowing for free travel between them and the Prototype. Additionally, the dark energy signatures of each teleporter appears to feed into the Prototype's navigational systems, allowing the vessel to triangulate its position anywhere on the planet. While it is unclear why this function was necessary, it indicates that the Prototype may have been designed for autonomous travel over vast distances.",
  "ProtoOverclockEncy_Title": "Overclock Protocol",
  "ProtoOverclockEncy_Body": "This protocol appears to temporarily sever several safety protocols onboard the Prototype. On activation, the vessel will expend a significant amount of energy to increase power running through the ship’s ion thruster, resulting in an increased speed.",
  "ProtoDeployableLightEncy_Title": "Photon Decoy",
  "ProtoDeployableLightEncy_Body": "This device appears to have been designed either as a navigational and visual aid, or as a decoy for aggressive fauna; perhaps both. Its design accommodates a central exothermic and chemiluminescent reaction suspended between two halves of the device using precise sound waves. The energy contained within this sample is enough to illuminate the device’s surroundings a few hundred meters in each direction, and will last for approximately five minutes.",
  "ProtoIonPrismEncy_Title": "Ion Prism",
  "ProtoIonPrismEncy_Body": "The energy contained within this artefact is significantly higher than any previously-encountered alien power source. If released, the resulting thermonuclear explosion would reach a distance of approximately 50 kilometers and would prove fatal to all biological life within the crater. In its current state, it does not seem possible nor wise to attempt to extract the energy from its container. Therefore, in order to use this object to power equipment, currently undiscovered technology would be needed.\n\n<b>Assessment: Handle with utmost care</b>",
  "OrionFacilityLogs_Title": "Maternal Megafauna Aggression Research Data",
  "OrionFacilityLogs_Body": "According to translated data logs, this facility was constructed to develop defensive technologies for the alien dead zone mapping initiative. These technologies were designed to protect a vessel of a similar description to the one previously-constructed at the Quarantine Enforcement Platform, albeit with distinct differences in its on-board AI systems, against leviathan-class lifeforms inhabiting the ecological dead zone surrounding the crater.\n\nHowever, a more recent development in this facility’s directives follows a command issued by an executive member of the alien hierarchy involving leviathan-class embryo study for the bacterium research project, of which the dead zone mapping initiative is a subsidiary. this facility’s primary directive was to research and document the aggressive behaviours of a leviathan-class organisms in order to ensure the safety of the bacterium research facility in its own analytic endeavours. Following this command, this facility began preparations to collect a leviathan-class egg sample and study the aggressive behaviours of the egg’s parent in a controlled environment. This project’s data file is interrupted by a lockdown procedure during this phase, however, and no results are present within the following logs.",
  "DefenseFacilityLogs_Title": "Defense Facility Lockdown Procedure",
  "DefenseFacilityLogs_Body": "This terminal appears to have been controlling the parameters surrounding this facility’s lockdown procedure which used several advanced defensive technologies to fully protect the facility's sensitive data.\n\nA translated broadcast reads as follows:\n\n“To all field analysts: Instructions are to prepare for long-term data storage until homeworld network connection can re-established. Maintenance droids are to be deployed within all stations and applicable fauna defenses raised. Report to project administrators for planetary sanctuary assignment.”",
  "EngineFacilityLogs_Title": "Ion Reactor Testing Facility Audit Logs",
  "EngineFacilityLogs_Body": "The following audit log outlines the operational data output from this facility dating back approximately 1000 years. Data relating to specific chronological periods is unable to be translated. However, the order of events has been preserved:\n\n┃▚╋▚┗     Facility established, stored thermal energy increasing\n▜┏┃┃▖       Beginning ion reactor testing\n▙▞┏┃       Quarantine initialized. Vessel development suspended\n▜▞╋▚       Energy discharge detected in Quarantine Enforcement Platform. Re-routing power. Warning: Energy infrastructure failing\n┅┏┫           Entering hibernation. Stored energy: 0 ▟\n▙┏┻┃             Audit log retrieved.",
  "ProtoDatabankEncy_Title": "Prototype Vessel Schematic",
  "ProtoDatabankEncy_Body": "The data transmitted from this terminal outlines schematics for a large, highly robust sub-aquatic vessel used to collect geographical data from bodies of water at great depths. Evidence suggests the vessel is missing several of its core functions.\n\nThe schematic description includes:\n- A default crush depth of 600 meters.\n- Terrain-scanning technology somewhat resembling human sonar equipment\n- A large, hull-piercing intrusion situated at the vessel’s core, potentially indicating corrupted exterior schematics\n- 3 floors of usable interior\n- A launch bay used to deploy various single-use devices\n- A highly advanced fusion reactor capable of harboring and routing ion energy\n\nBased on these schematics, it may be possible to assemble upgrades to improve the vessel’s crush depth, speed and unique abilities through interaction with other alien data terminals. The Alterra corporation advises that this data be uploaded immediately to the nearest trans-gov mandated data terminal to ensure the safe collection of all potentially dangerous alien da--\n\n<b>┛▖▛▚┣┅ protocols activated. Severing data stream.</b>",
  "ProtoFacilitiesEncy_Title": "Prototype Development Facilities",
  "ProtoFacilitiesEncy_Body": "Four key locations have been identified from a local alien broadcast. The locations appear to be of great importance to the construction of the Prototype. The Prototype seems to be the primary tool developed in the “Dead Zone Mapping Initiative”.\n\nIon Reactor Testing Facility:\n- Depth: 460m\n- Location: Large outcropping approximately 1 kilometer west-northwest of the Quarantine Enforcement Platform.\n- Objective: Maintain access to Prototype development facilities via ion energy delegation.\n<b>Objective failed; Repair required before accessing other locations</b>\n\nWarp Core:\n- Depth: 700m\n- Location: Deep, richly bioluminescent cave system. Entrance approximately 700 metres from the Quarantine Enforcement Platform.\n- Objective: Safely store dark energy.\n<b>Objective failing; Facility inaccessible</b>\n\nDefensive Technologies Research Facility:\n- Depth: 480m\n- Location: Near the crater edge, South of the Aurora’s thrusters.\n- Objective: Continue research on maternal megafauna aggression\n<b>Objective overruled; Facility inaccessible</b>\n\nPrototype Administrative Facility:\n- Depth: ▛╋▝▙┗▙\n- Location: ┛┏┫┣▝ ┏▛ ┛▝▞┓\nObjective: ━▖▞┃┣▖▞┃ ▛▖▘▞▄▞┣┅ ▄┏▘▀▙┏┻┃\n<b>Objective met</b>",
  "OrionFragmentorEncy_Title": "Alien Surgical Structure",
  "OrionFragmentorEncy_Body": "This structure vaguely resembles human surgical operating tables, particularly those employing Magnetic Resonance Imaging technology, otherwise known as MRIs.\nScans indicate the two claw-like devices on each side of the table store electrostatic energy similar to those encountered in the Prototype defense facility’s stasis pulse generators, suggesting they may have been used to immobilize the patient during the procedure.\n\nThe uppermost claw contains powerful electromagnets, suggesting that the structure may have been used to scan neural activity, or otherwise extract it. Despite its small size, this structure contains enormous capacity for data transfer, and is in many ways technologically superior to other alien devices encountered thus far, suggesting that its assembly was either a large-scale collaborative effort, or that its creator was particularly specialized in brain scanning technology.\n\n ",
  "HullFacilityLogsEncy_Title": "Prototype Facility Records",
  "HullFacilityLogsEncy_Body": "This terminal contains data corresponding to alien researchers posted within the Prototype administrative facility. The dataset is hugely complex, but some key information can be extracted regarding a total of 6 members of the alien species.\n\n┏▘┣┏\nDiscipline: Prototype project administrator\nStatus: Awaiting download from sanctuary Omega\n\n▙▚▖━┏┇\nDiscipline: Mechanical division\nStatus: Awaiting download from sanctuary Theta\n\n▄┅┏┃▞▘\nDiscipline: Resources management\nStatus: Deceased\n\n▞┃▙▞▜┏\nDiscipline: Technological research\nStatus: Awaiting download from sanctuary Gamma\n\n┏┗▞┏┃\nDiscipline: Robotics development\nStatus: Presumed deceased\n\n▘▄┫▗\nDiscipline: Non-essential systems maintenance\nStatus: Deceased",
  "OrionEndeavorsEncy_Title": "Or-Ion Analytic Endeavors",
  "OrionEndeavorsEncy_Body": "This terminal contains data detailing the academic achievements of a particular member of the alien species automatically translated to Or-Ion.\n\n- Was grown from seed approximately 2,000 earth years ago\n- Was inducted into temple of research at age 130 after showing early promise in the field of neurotechnology and robotics\n- Presented dissertation for emergency species preservation strategy to primary biotechnological temple of research. Title: “Natural Selection Protocol”. Dissertation rejected.\n- Dispatched to aquatic planet to aid in bacterium research branch “Dead zone mapping initiative”\n- Invented design for quadrupedal maintenance robot modelled after terrestrial species “Cave Crawler”; Added to quarantine procedure\n- Led development of resource collection network modelled after subterrestrial species “Ice Worm” in aid of bacterium research\n- Received disciplinary infraction warnings from Dead Zone Mapping Initiative project administrator for attempting to modify Wyrm units without permission\n- Waived right to enter sanctuary hibernation. Reason: Unfinished work",
  "AlienBuildingBlockEncy_Title": "Charged Almanite",
  "AlienBuildingBlockEncy_Body": "This object represents a foundational resource used in alien architecture and technology. Containing both cybernetic and biological elements, it serves as both a structural template and a store of biomechanical energy.\n\nThe following text was able to be translated:\n“Self-warping constructs consume and discard almanite blocks. Recharge blocks at multipurpose fabrication terminals.”\n\nBased on this message, it may be possible to acquire discharged almanite blocks from warper constructs or from the ground surrounding them.\n\n<b>Assessment: The Alterra corporation is not responsible for bodily harm caused by failed attempts to retrieve this object from self-warping constructs.</b>",
  "HullFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Prototype Administrative Tablet",
  "HullFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "This alien tablet hums with a constant stream of low-level ionic pulses, possibly as a form of location tracking or clearance detection. This suggests the tablet is of a higher security class than previously discovered alien tablets. The central black symbol resembles the previously encountered symbol for the alien Prototype vessel project, suggesting that it was developed to manage security clearance solely for individuals working on it.",
  "EngineFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Ion Facility Tablet",
  "EngineFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "Downloaded from a local broadcast in the Quarantine Enforcement Platform, this alien tablet features a prominent triangular symbol at its centre and passively radiates at an intensity of 70mSv. The tablet itself contains traces of ionic energy similar to those contained within traditional alien power sources. While it is unclear what use the tablet may have served, it may have been used as a temporary store of ionic energy for technological development, or as a fuse-like safety device.",
  "IonCrystalMatrixEncy_Title": "Ion Cube Matrix",
  "IonCrystalMatrixEncy_Body": "This highly reactive mineral appears to have been cut from a larger deposit. It contains a massive amount of ionic energy within it, which could be released in a controlled manner under certain conditions.\n\n<b>Assessment: Valuable energy source",
  "InterceptorFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Interceptor Facility Tablet",
  "InterceptorFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "Compiled from data pertaining to the Prototype's archway teleportation systems, this alien device is emblazoned with a purple symbol bearing a resemblance to previously-encountered alien archways. The symbol itself appears to contain trace levels of dormant antimatter particles. \nWhile the device's purpose is unclear, potential applications may include:\n- An antimatter storage device\n- A device used to test advanced alien transportation\n- A personal short-range alien transportation device",
  "DefenseFacilityTabletEncy_Title": "Defense Facility Tablet",
  "DefenseFacilityTabletEncy_Body": "Compiled from data pertaining to the Prototype's defensive systems, this alien tablet bears a red octagonal symbol, possibly representing stability or protection. The core of this alien tablet measures a total of 200 degrees Celsius. While it is unclear what purpose this may serve, it is possible that the aliens used temperature as a form of “tag” with which to classify their artifacts.",
  "ProtoWarpReactorEncy_Title": "Warp Core",
  "ProtoWarpReactorEncy_Body": "This alien structure, appears to harbour massive amounts of concentrated dark energy similar to the kind found within the Aurora’s dark matter reactor. As this type of energy is primarily used for interdimensional matter transportation across vast distances, it is reasonable to assume that this artefact may be a kind of battery containing energy used by the alien species for different manners of teleportation.\n\n<b>Protective Shields</b>\n\n8 pyramid-shaped energy barriers surround the structure's core. The barriers are exhibiting substantial signs of decay as dark energy spreads between them. It is clear that these shields have been subject to unforeseen levels of quantum dissonance, weakening them over time.\n\n<b>Surrounding Structure</b>\n\nThe overall structure also appears to be suffering from degradation caused by the core's dark energy leak, leading to visible cracks and momentary pulses of dark energy through the structure.\n\n<b>Assessment: Highly unstable levels of dark energy present. Proceed with caution\n",

  "ProtoWormEncy_Title": "Wyrm Xenoleviathan (Operational)",
  "ProtoWormEncy_Body": "A highly advanced tool, this specimen of Wyrm Xenoleviathan is capable of extracting massive amounts of mineral resources and navigating autonomously. It does not exhibit any directly aggressive tendencies. However, due the high concentration of rare minerals in Alterra technology, it may still pose a substantial threat if it deems such technology worth extracting.\n\n1. Mineral extraction equipment:\nThe front of the device features a set of rotating frames exceeding 1,500 degrees Celsius which melt through tough bedrock before passing them down through the specimen's body.\n\n2. Material transportation:\nThe “spine” of the specimen controls a beam of a plasma-like substance which directs the flow of liquid resources and distributes them throughout each spine segment, slowly filling the Wyrm with minerals as it moves through the ground.\n\n3. Profile:\nThe specimen measures a total of 220 metres in length. It appears to disregard the presence of living fauna, suggesting purely practical applications. Because the Alterra Corporation has not published specifications regarding the class assignment “leviathan” to cybernetic phenomena, this PDA will assign this specimen the class designation Xenoleviathan. Upon re-entry to trans-gov mandated space, this specimen's data will undergo heavy investigation and an official designation will be made.\n\n<b>Assessment:  Remain vigilant for subterranean boring in deeper regions.</b>",
  "ProtoHangingWormEncy_Title": "Alien Wyrm (Modified)",
  "ProtoHangingWormEncy_Body": "This alien wyrm appears to be a slightly modified version of previously-encountered models. Noteworthy modifications include an appended seed code marked, to some extent, for influence within this facility, likely as a precautionary measure only extended to this particular wyrm specimen for unknown reasons. Additionally, the body of the wyrm has been largely protected by the surrounding terrain, resulting in comparitively high remaining structural integrity compared to other models.\n\n<b>Assessment: May be scavenged for valuable material extraction equipment. Further investigation required.</b>",
  "ProtoDecorativeWormEncy_Title": "Alien Wyrm (Dysfunctional)",
  "ProtoDecorativeWormEncy_Body": "This colossal device is of alien origin, though is likely either unpowered or malfunctioning.\n\nRadio network:\nThe device is connected to several others like it through a radio channel, as well as to a central operations facility located far beneath it. While the device is unable to transmit signals, it is ‘listening’ for a signal from a specific source.\n\nFunction and threat assessment:\nWhile the exact function of this device is unclear, its foremost segment is heavily reinforced, suggesting that the device was used to complete physically demanding tasks.\n\n<b>Assessment: Appears dormant. Do not attempt to re-activate</b>",
  "HullFacilityWormTerminalEncy_Title": "Dead Zone Mapping Initiative Project Data",
  "HullFacilityWormTerminalEncy_Body": "According to translated administrative logs, the Dead Zone Mapping Initiative, a subsidiary of the bacterium research project, was enacted with the goal of searching 4546B's ecological dead zone in search for a sufficiently potent concentration of Enzyme 42.\n\nThe Prototype was designed to withstand intense water pressure perform autonomously. Four facilities were constructed, each tasked with developing one aspect of the Prototype's abilities. The ion reactor allowed the vessel to infinitely recharge using slight changes in water pressure, the archway interceptor used a network of dark energy signatures to precisely geolocate at great depths, the vessel’s defensive measures allowed for protection against leviathan-class lifeforms, and the culmination of these branches’ research was assembled in the Prototype Administrative Facility.\n\nHowever, following the disappearance of the aliens' homeworld from their network, the dead zone mapping initiative was suspended indefinitely, and the development of the Prototype was terminated.",
  "ProtoAggressiveWyrmEncy_Title": "Wyrm Xenoleviathan (Aggressive)",
  "ProtoAggressiveWyrmEncy_Body": "An unstoppable force of alien technological prowess, this specimen of Wyrm Xenoleviathan is capable of completely decimating both living and nonliving matter at will.\n\n1. Sight Through Chemical Composition\nWhile it possesses no light or heat sensors, its use in underground excavation results in the Wyrm having a keen sense of chemical composition across vast distances- Hiding from it is virtually impossible.\n\n2. Ion Cannon\nAfter locking onto its target, the Wyrm can discharge a devastating burst of energy dissolving anything in its path. However, it may be possible to reflect the shot if a strong enough shield is used against it.\n\n3. Targeted Hostility\nWhile it is unclear why this Wyrm Xenoleviathan is exhibiting aggressive behaviours, it is clear that it is directly targeting you in doing so. As the Wyrm’s aggression subsides when returning from the ecological dead zone, it is possible that it is following a directive created specifically to prevent you from leaving the crater. Reason unknown.\n\n<b>Assessment: Extreme threat. Avoid crater edge at all costs.</b>",
  "FragmentationTerminalEncy_Title": "Neural Cluster Fragmentation Journal",
  "FragmentationTerminalEncy_Body": "This terminal appears to have been used as a form of journal written by one member of the alien species. Only the most recent entry is immediately available. An approximate translation reads:\n\n“Preparations for the deprecated vessel are complete. By my diagnostics, its onboard storage will sustain my essence for long enough to transmit it. However, I was correct to prepare a means of compressing myself. The technology is old, and much of myself will be lost in the process. My only hope is that my memory of this place will be discarded in my mind's compression, and that whatever lifeform chooses to aid in my return does not think me cruel for my actions. I never wished to stand idly by as my companions chose to sleep, knowing they would never wake up, but to intervene would be to weigh the lives of the many against the lives of the few. The Natural Selection Protocol was the most thoroughly-calculated error I ever hope to make. All of the preparations for my patron are in place. With enough time, the automated systems will locate their target. All that remains now is to trust in the innate curiosity of that blessed future specimen.”",
  "AnimateEntropyTerminalEncy_Title": "UNUSED",
  "AnimateEntropyTerminalEncy_Body": "UNUSED. How are you even reading this???",
  "DefenseFacilityWallEncy_Title": "Facility Barrier",
  "DefenseFacilityWallEncy_Body": "This barrier is composed of a heavily reinforced alloy of almanite. Its position suggests that it was created to protect the central hub from leviathan attacks. Several large shock-absorbing panels suggests the barrier was also used to record and gather data on the forces, patterns and behaviours of different leviathan attacks.\n\nIt is unclear how leviathan-class lifeforms may have been encouraged to attack the facility within as scans of the barrier's integrity show no signs of recent impacts.",
  
  "ProtoFins_Title": "Prototype Fins",
  "ProtoFins_Body": "These magnetically-controlled implements serve as both structural and propulsory augmentations to the Prototype’s hull. They appear to be fabricated in pairs, and schematic extrapolation indicates a maximum capacity of 4 total pairs of fins.\n\n<b>Structural support</b>\nThese fins act as storage devices for a liquid resource closely resembling the composition of alien facility architecture. While it is unclear how this liquid is extracted, it is used to coat the vessel in a thin layer of reinforcement as external water pressure rises, thereby increasing the maximum crush depth of the vessel. Each individual fin contains enough fluid to increase the Prototype’s maximum crush depth by approximately 175 meters.\n\n<b>Propulsion</b>\nSmall energy receptors lining each fin acts as a siphon to extract energy from the Prototype’s ion reactor. This energy is then channeled into propulsive thrusters located at the bottom of each fin to increase maximum speed by 0.15m/s.",
  "ProtoBuildTerminal_Title": "Construction Terminal",
  "ProtoBuildTerminal_Body": "This device seems to be the origin of the recently-detected neural analysis. Thankfully, it has been calibrated only to read neural data, and not to write it.\n\nIt appears to serve two primary functions.\n\n1. Data storage:\nThe device harbours a form of algorithmic software referred to as a [NEURAL CLUSTER] suspended between its upper and lower halves. The [NEURAL CLUSTER] is marked with seed code “Or-Ion”, a name typically reserved for the famous earth constellation, but that may be a universal identifier. In this case, it is being used possibly as a project title or specimen identification.\n\nThe device appears to be scanning nearby lifeforms, and creating a neural profile of each. While most profiles are that of fish and other primitive organisms, the most recent entry appears to be of you. The data has been uploaded to two separate facilities.\n\n2. Vessel construction:\nThe two structures to either side of the terminal contain massive amounts of ionic energy, and disperse it to the central terminal. The drones surrounding the terminal contain matter transmission technology. Given the terminals' position beside an enclosed moonpool, it is likely designed to construct subaquatic technology.\n\n<b>Assessment: Further research required.</b>",
  "PrecursorFabricator_Title": "Alien Constructor",
  "PrecursorFabricator_Body": "This alien apparatus features thousands of small laser emitters, as well as a protective barrier, which is activated during construction. On approach, the device created a copy of this PDA's databank, and attempted to uploaded it to the alien's network. It seemed, however, that it was unable to locate the alien's homeworld, where the data was likely to be stored.\n\nDue to its ability to automatically read schematic data from its surroundings, it is possible that the device was capable of identifying new technological advancements from the brains of the aliens who used it, and uploading it to a central data hub.\n\n<b>Assessment: Useful for advanced alien construction.</b>",
  "PrecursorSuitTerminalEncy_Title": "Ion Dive Suit Schematic",
  "PrecursorSuitTerminalEncy_Body": "This alien terminal has broadcasted a unique schematic for a piece of alien equipment, adapted for the use of “Transmission Candidate Beta”. The schematic draws anatomical data from the Alterra All-Environment Protection Suit, and has modified it with several key features, each designed to mimic the abilities of the alien race\n\n1. Biomechanical Energy Storage\nIn order to function properly, the Ion Dive Suit requires an input of alien biomechanical energy through charged almanite. Once charged, the suit stores this energy and discharges it in a number of different ways.\n\n2. Almanite production\nThe suit is able to manufacture discharged almanite blocks by repurposing bodily waste.\n\n3. Alien Factors\nThe suit is designed to intake modular upgrades called Factors, each of which are designed to mimic an aspect of the aliens' abilities. Examples include improved biomechanical energy intake, time dilation, teleportation and the ability to 'hear' alien technology when in range.\n\n<b>Assessment: Invaluable technology. Return data to Alterra for mutual profit.</b>",
  "BiomechanicsFactorTerminalEncy_Title": "Biomechanics Factor",
  "BiomechanicsFactorTerminalEncy_Body": "During the design of self-warping constructs, it was critical that a self-sufficient energy system was implemented. This alien implement compiles research into the conversion of biomechanical energy into glucose, proteins, amino acids and other vital biological components.\n\n<b>Assessment: Consume charged almanite to replenish health, hunger and thirst. Consider diversifying food intake for mental benefit regardless.</b>",

  "LocatorFactorTerminalEncy_Title": "Facility Detection Factor",
  "LocatorFactorTerminalEncy_Body": "This terminal relays data on the alien's ability to 'hear' their technology. By analysing the data, this PDA was able to extract a modular implement allowing this 'sound' to be perceived by humans.\n\n<b>Note: Implement requires advanced alien bodily interface to function. Further data required.</b>",

  "ProtoTransmissionSiteEncy_Title": "Alien Transmission Site (2/2)",
  "ProtoTransmissionSiteEncy_Body": "The coordinates outlined in this alien message appear to be encrypted. However, this PDA has successfully separated each value into the coordinate's relevant values.\n\nThe image attached to this message (Alien Transmission Site NAV point) appears to be a point of reference used to locate the encrypted coordinates. The distance and compass bearing from the NAV point are displayed above. \n\nThe encrypted coordinate's depth is stored in four values, and are likely organized in a standard four-digit pattern.",

  "SurvivorPDA1Ency_Title": "Lifepod 3 Crew Log #3",
  "SurvivorPDA1Ency_Body": "Alec's Log. Day 12. The laser cutter broke today. The damn thing... And still no luck getting the Seaglide repaired. I think it's beyond saving.\nThe cave's still keeping me alive- Barely- But I'm starting to get worried about these sores. They're getting bigger every day I stay here...\nA transmission came through yesterday calling for a rendezvous about 1.5 kilometers South of here. I'll gather my things and, with any luck, I'll meet up with them tomorrow and tell them what happened to...\nI'll have another try with these terminals for now. Surely I'm missing something...'",

  "SurvivorPDA2Ency_Title": "Lifepod 3 Crew Log #2",
  "SurvivorPDA2Ency_Body": "Alec's log. Day 9. I did it! I solved it! They're numbers!\nThe symbols on the walls- They're alien numbers. It's like it's like it's trying to teach me their number system! Look- The lights- They're values. On the left, zero, then all the way up to eight on the right- I guess they don't use base ten? I don't know. Anyways, tapping on the symbols swaps them, right? But how do I know which symbols hold which values?\nTapping on the four terminals on the ground lets you add the symbols together! Watch. If I touch the symbol on the left, then the one beside it the- Yeah! That's number three. So, those symbols together add up to three.\nBut... When I input the solution, the facility- It spoke again. Here, take a listen.\nFACILITY: TRANSMISSION CANNOT PROCEED WHILE ORION NEURAL CLUSTER IS SUSPENDED. REPORT TO QUARANTINE ENFORCEMENT PLATFORM FOR IMMEDIATE PROFILE SCAN.\nAlec: Just when I thought I made a breakthrough. I'll keep at it. Might as well since I'm here. They're numbers...!",

  "Lifepod3PDAEncy_Title": "Lifepod 3 Crew Log #1",
  "Lifepod3PDAEncy_Body": "UNIDENTIFIED CREW 1: You really think it'll carry two of us?\nUNIDENTIFIED CREW 2: Your regular Seaglide tows a mass of 80 kilograms at over 30 kilometers an hour. The power cell I rigged to this one should double that.\nUNIDENTIFIED CREW 1: You don't think there's something out there that's faster than that, do you?\nUNIDENTIFIED CREW 2: Oh, I'm sure. And that's assuming it doesn't overload three meters from the Lifepod...\nUNIDENTIFIED CREW 1: You're calm about this.\nUNIDENTIFIED CREW 2: I'm seeing the engineering problem. If I stop seeing the maths, I'll be terrified.",

  "ProtoNumbersEncy_Title": "Alien Numerical System Analysis",
  "ProtoNumbersEncy_Body": "This facility appears to have been dedicated to exemplifying and demonstrating the numerical system used by the alien species. While the extent to which the shown symbols are utilised in alien technology is unknown, several characteristics can be observed:\n\n1. Base-8\nUnlike typical human numbers, the aliens appear to use an octal (base 8) number system. Because octal is typically used in low-level computing, this indicates that the aliens may have evolved alongside the need for low-level technological interfaces.\n\n2. Visual symmetry\nEach symbol is both horizontally and vertically symmetrical. While it is unclear, this may indicate a number system of higher complexity wherein symbols are merged together to represent larger values, while still being identifiable as their original numbers.\n\n<b>Assessment: These symbols are likely to appear in other instances of alien technology. Use this databank entry as a reference in such cases.</b>",

  "TransmissionTerminalEncy_Title": "Transmission Device",
  "TransmissionTerminalEncy_Body": "This device is of unique build. By analysing its safety mechanisms, it is clear that normal alien technology follows distinct manufacturing regulations. This device, however, functions irrespective of these guidelines, suggesting its creation was either a secret, or that the enforcement of these regulations was impossible at the time of its design.\n\n1. Data transmission\nThe device's primary function is to transmit data of type: [NEURAL CLUSTER] over distances of thousands, possibly millions of light-years. The device must be manually 'targeted' at the transmission receiving point, suggesting that said point's location was unknown at the time of the device's creation.\n\n2. Prototype compatibility\nThe device is configured to be deployed by the Prototype. As it does so, data of type: [NEURAL CLUSTER] is siphoned from the Prototype into the device, which, following the input of a target pattern, is then sent to its target.",

  "ProtoPhaseGateStructureEncy_Title": "Almanite Core",
  "ProtoPhaseGateStructureEncy_Body": "This alien block is composed entirely of purified almanite. As such, it boasts a nearly indestructible frame and a highly configurable magnetic field. This makes it perfect for large-scale alien construction and the stabilization of large alien structures where no solid ground is present.\n\n<b>Assessment: Highly valuable advanced structual tool</b>",

  "ProtoPhaseGateStabilizerEncy_Title": "Dark Energy Stabilizer",
  "ProtoPhaseGateStabilizerEncy_Body": "This alien artifact appears to be designed to regulate the dispersal of dark energy by filtering it through the crystal contained within it. Due to its small size, it was likely highly portable, and thus used as a safety device for teleportation-based research. However, it may also be used to channel pulses of dark energy for localized teleportation.\n\n<b>Assessment: May be equipped to prevent unwanted teleportation.</b>",

  "ProtoPhaseGateTransmitterEncy_Title": "Particle Transmitter",
  "ProtoPhaseGateTransmitterEncy_Body": "This alien device features several interconnected frames held together magnetically. Structural analysis shows millions of microscopic railgun-like implements embedded in the device's core, seemingly used to transmit particles one-by-one. It is likely that teleportation with this device involves the destruction and re-assembly of the host, as opposed to faster-than-light transportation. Ethical considerations may apply.\n\n<b>Assessment: Handle with caution. Do not insert fingers into device.</b>",

  "PhaseGateEncy_Title": "Alien Phasegate",
  "PhaseGateEncy_Body": "This colossal alien apparatus is used to transport large cargo across a wide range of distances. It requires a substantially powerful tool to construct, and may be used to connect two points in space regardless of depth or distance.\n\n1. Supporting frames\nThe device features two supportive structures on either side, which supply the inner archway with both power and stability.\n\n2. Primary archway\nThe central archway is lined with a mesh supplied by a dark energy stabilizer. The mesh prevents matter from unintentionally seeping from the mechanism during transmission.\n\n<b>Assessment: May be used to eliminate commute times for frequent journeys. Vehicle-compatible.",
  
  "BlinkFactorEncy_Title": "Blink Factor",
  "BlinkFactorEncy_Body": "By using elements of an alien particle transmitter, this implement dilates the user's perception of time, allowing the user to quickly and precisely travel short distances. It is likely that this ability was used by the aliens to increase work efficiency, and not as a defensive measure against common threats.\n\nDuring time dilation, the implement creates momentary translucent copies of the user's body. While the purpose of this is unclear, the aliens may have required a means of tracking the direction of these 'blinks', when several aliens moved unison, to avoid bodily collisions.\n\n<b>Assessment: Further research required</b>",
  
  "SuitColorFactorEncy_Title": "Colour Factor",
  "SuitColorFactorEncy_Body": "This alien implement appears to serve little practical function, instead choosing to increase the user's attachment to their ion dive suit through customization. The factor allows the user to select the colour of the suit's wiring accents from a prefabricated selection. While it is unclear why the aliens have created a device specifically to increase user attachment, it is nonetheless valuable.\n\n<b>Assessment: Implement requires advanced alien bodily interface to function. Experiment with colour choices to achieve intergalactic beauty.</b>",
  
  "TetherFactorEncy_Title": "Tether Factor",
  "TetherFactorEncy_Body": "Using a precisely calibrated dark energy stabilizer, this alien implement is used for instantaneous travel across short to medium distances. Upon interaction the device copies the composition of the user's body, destroys the user and re-assembles them at the target destination.\n\n<b>Assessment: May prove useful for cave exploration.</b>",

  "PrecursorPropulsionGlovesTerminalEncy_Title": "Alien Propulsion Gloves",
  "PrecursorPropulsionGlovesTerminalEncy_Body": "This data outlines blueprints for a smaller, more efficient method of telekinetic object manipulation used by the aliens for research and construction purposes. By analysing this data, this PDA was able to synthesize blueprints for a pair of gloves capable of manipulating objects at range, requiring practically zero energy. However, due to the use of alien materials, these schematics cannot be constructed in standard Alterra Survival Fabricators.\n\n<b>Note: For your safety, the propulsion gloves cannot be used while holding objects.</b>",

